First, Bob needs to calculate how many boxes of popsicles he needs. He needs 56 popsicle sticks, and each box contains 8 sticks.  So he needs 56 / 8 = 7 boxes.

Next, Bob needs to calculate the total cost. Each box costs $2.00, and he needs 7 boxes.  So the total cost is 7 * $2.00 = $14.00.

